From: Leo Audio OS <leo-audio-os@localhost>
Date: 2026-08-29
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] leo: add bypass detection, status and safe fallback

Completes the controller with the parts that decide whether the system may
claim HiFi at all.

WCD bypass observation.  The chain is

    MultiMediaN -> SLIMBUS_0_RX -> SLIM RXn MUX -> RXn MIX1 INP1
                -> CLASS_H_DSM MUX -> HPHL DAC Switch -> jack

and the assertion now distinguishes an audible path from a harmless one:

  * FATAL, and only fatal: HPHL DAC Switch is On.  That is the analog
    outlet, and M2 proved on the real device that cutting it silences the
    WCD path even while SLIMBUS_0_RX <- MultiMedia5 is still On.
  * RECORDED, not fatal: a live front end, mux, interpolator input or
    Class-H mux with the outlet cut.  That is a bypass *attempt*: worth
    reporting, but not proof of sound.

The earlier draft treated any SLIMBUS front end as fatal.  That was too
strict: because hw_interface_table puts the ESS on its own backend,
check_and_route_playback_usecases() deliberately leaves other usecases on
SLIMBUS, so a notification stream would have killed HiFi outright.

Right-channel coverage: this sound card exposes only one "HPHL DAC
Switch"; the right DAC is gated through the RX2 chain and CLASS_H_DSM MUX,
so those are observed too (as optional controls, absent-tolerant).

New evidence bit E4: at least one QUAT_MI2S_RX Audio Mixer MultiMediaN
must read back On.  Only four usecases have a "<usecase> hifi-headphones"
path in mixer_paths.xml, so a usecase without one would apply no path at
all and silently produce silence; E4 is what catches that.

State machine: every route change starts a new generation and clears the
evidence bitmap, so stale evidence can never promote a state; HIFI_ACTIVE
requires the full fatal mask; a missing E7 (volume read-back) degrades
instead of failing; the unified fallback restores the backend, returns
"Volume" to 205 and lands in ERROR_FALLBACK, which cannot become
HIFI_ACTIVE without a new generation and a fresh full read-back.  A route
back to a non-HiFi device clears ERROR_FALLBACK to WIRED_STANDARD, so an
ordinary headphone route is never reported as a system error.

get_parameters("leo_hifi_status") exposes the snapshot read-only, ACDB
reported as absent_expected.
Baseline: MoKee/android_hardware_qcom_audio
          mkq-mr1-caf-msm8994 @ 7f4cac748b6f62897294cdaece9d1aec27e1e927
---
--- a/hal/msm8974/leo_hifi.h
+++ b/hal/msm8974/leo_hifi.h
@@ -232,6 +232,66 @@
 
 /* Exit-side hook called from disable_audio_route(); never blocks teardown. */
 void platform_leo_hifi_backend_exit(void *platform, int snd_device);
+
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------- *
+ * WCD bypass detection, state machine and read-only status
+ * ---------------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* Evidence bits, mirrored into the leo_hifi_status string. */
+#define LEO_EV_E2       (1u << 1)   /* HiFi snd_device selected               */
+#define LEO_EV_E3       (1u << 2)   /* ES9018 bound on I2C 6-0048             */
+#define LEO_EV_E4       (1u << 3)   /* a QUAT_MI2S_RX front end is On         */
+#define LEO_EV_E5       (1u << 4)   /* no complete WCD path to the jack       */
+#define LEO_EV_E6       (1u << 5)   /* QUAT backend read back as targeted     */
+#define LEO_EV_E7       (1u << 6)   /* ES9018 Volume read back as expected    */
+#define LEO_EV_E9       (1u << 7)   /* no control write failure this gen      */
+
+#define LEO_EV_FATAL_MASK \
+    (LEO_EV_E2 | LEO_EV_E3 | LEO_EV_E4 | LEO_EV_E5 | LEO_EV_E6 | LEO_EV_E9)
+
+/*
+ * Bypass observation bits.  These describe the WCD9330 chain
+ *   MultiMediaN -> SLIMBUS_0_RX -> SLIM RXn MUX -> RXn MIX1 INP1
+ *                -> CLASS_H_DSM MUX -> HPHL DAC Switch -> jack
+ * Only LEO_BP_OUTLET is fatal on its own: M2 proved on the real device that
+ * cutting the analog outlet silences the WCD path even while
+ * SLIMBUS_0_RX <- MultiMedia5 is still On.  Everything else is recorded as a
+ * bypass *attempt*, which is diagnostic, not proof of audible sound.
+ */
+#define LEO_BP_SLIM_FE  (1u << 0)   /* some SLIMBUS_0_RX <- MultiMediaN On    */
+#define LEO_BP_MUX_LIVE (1u << 1)   /* SLIM RX1 or RX2 MUX != ZERO            */
+#define LEO_BP_MIX_LIVE (1u << 2)   /* RX1 or RX2 MIX1 INP1 != ZERO           */
+#define LEO_BP_CLASSH   (1u << 3)   /* CLASS_H_DSM MUX != ZERO                */
+#define LEO_BP_OUTLET   (1u << 4)   /* HPHL DAC Switch On -- FATAL            */
 
+#define LEO_BP_FATAL_MASK   (LEO_BP_OUTLET)
 
+/*
+ * Observe the WCD chain.  Returns true when no FATAL bypass condition is
+ * present.  Always fills lh->bypass with everything it saw, so a non-fatal
+ * "bypass attempt" is visible in the status string without changing state.
+ *
+ * This is only meaningful while the HiFi device is selected.  In the ordinary
+ * WIRED_STANDARD case the WCD chain is supposed to be live, and the state
+ * machine does not call this at all.
+ */
+bool leo_hifi_check_bypass(struct leo_hifi *lh);
+
+/*
+ * State machine entry points.  leo_hifi_on_route() runs the full read-back
+ * sequence and decides between HIFI_ACTIVE, HIFI_DEGRADED and
+ * ERROR_FALLBACK; it never advances to HIFI_ACTIVE on stale evidence because
+ * every call starts a new generation and re-reads everything.
+ */
+void leo_hifi_on_route(struct leo_hifi *lh, bool to_hifi_device);
+void leo_hifi_on_route_off(struct leo_hifi *lh);
+
+/* Render the read-only status snapshot into buf (never fails). */
+void leo_hifi_status_string(struct leo_hifi *lh, char *buf, size_t len);
+
+/* Thin wrappers defined in platform.c and called from audio_hw.c. */
+void platform_leo_hifi_route_enabled(void *platform, int snd_device);
+void platform_leo_hifi_route_disabled(void *platform, int snd_device);
+
+
 #endif /* LEO_HIFI_H */
--- a/hal/msm8974/leo_hifi.c
+++ b/hal/msm8974/leo_hifi.c
@@ -421,4 +421,244 @@
           old ? "true" : "false", enable ? "true" : "false", lh->supported);
 
     return (old != enable);
+}
+
+static const char *leo_state_name(leo_hifi_state_t s)
+{
+    switch (s) {
+    case LEO_HIFI_IDLE:            return "idle";
+    case LEO_HIFI_SPEAKER:         return "speaker";
+    case LEO_HIFI_WIRED_STANDARD:  return "wired_standard";
+    case LEO_HIFI_ARMING:          return "arming";
+    case LEO_HIFI_ACTIVE:          return "hifi_active";
+    case LEO_HIFI_DEGRADED:        return "hifi_degraded";
+    case LEO_HIFI_ERROR_FALLBACK:  return "error_fallback";
+    default:                       return "unknown";
+    }
+}
+
+/* An enum control counts as "live" when it is resolvable and not ZERO. */
+static bool leo_enum_is_live(struct mixer_ctl *ctl)
+{
+    const char *s;
+    int idx;
+
+    if (ctl == NULL)
+        return false;
+
+    idx = mixer_ctl_get_value(ctl, 0);
+    if (idx < 0)
+        return false;
+
+    s = mixer_ctl_get_enum_string(ctl, (unsigned int)idx);
+    return (s != NULL && strcmp(s, "ZERO") != 0);
+}
+
+bool leo_hifi_check_bypass(struct leo_hifi *lh)
+{
+    unsigned int bp = 0;
+    int i;
+    int v;
+
+    /* (1) digital front end feeding the WCD backend */
+    for (i = 0; i < LEO_HIFI_MM_COUNT; i++) {
+        if (lh->ctl_slim_mm[i] == NULL)
+            continue;
+        v = mixer_ctl_get_value(lh->ctl_slim_mm[i], 0);
+        if (v > 0) {
+            ALOGD("%s: SLIMBUS_0_RX Audio Mixer MultiMedia%d is On",
+                  __func__, i + 1);
+            bp |= LEO_BP_SLIM_FE;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /* (2) SLIM receive muxes, both channels */
+    if (leo_enum_is_live(lh->ctl_slim_rx1_mux) ||
+        leo_enum_is_live(lh->ctl_slim_rx2_mux))
+        bp |= LEO_BP_MUX_LIVE;
+
+    /* (3) interpolator inputs, both channels (optional controls) */
+    if (leo_enum_is_live(lh->ctl_rx1_mix1_inp1) ||
+        leo_enum_is_live(lh->ctl_rx2_mix1_inp1))
+        bp |= LEO_BP_MIX_LIVE;
+
+    /* (4) Class-H DSM mux -- this is what gates the RIGHT channel DAC */
+    if (leo_enum_is_live(lh->ctl_class_h_mux))
+        bp |= LEO_BP_CLASSH;
+
+    /* (5) the analog outlet itself: the decisive gate */
+    if (lh->ctl_hphl_dac != NULL) {
+        v = mixer_ctl_get_value(lh->ctl_hphl_dac, 0);
+        if (v > 0)
+            bp |= LEO_BP_OUTLET;
+    }
+
+    lh->bypass = bp;
+
+    if (bp & LEO_BP_FATAL_MASK) {
+        ALOGE("%s: FATAL WCD bypass: the analog outlet is open "
+              "(bypass mask 0x%x)", __func__, bp);
+        lh->fail_code = LEO_FAIL_WCD_BYPASS;
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    if (bp != 0)
+        ALOGW("%s: bypass attempt observed but the analog outlet is cut "
+              "(mask 0x%x); not audible, recorded only", __func__, bp);
+
+    return true;
+}
+
+static bool leo_quat_front_end_live(struct leo_hifi *lh)
+{
+    int i;
+    int v;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < LEO_HIFI_MM_COUNT; i++) {
+        if (lh->ctl_quat_mm[i] == NULL)
+            continue;
+        v = mixer_ctl_get_value(lh->ctl_quat_mm[i], 0);
+        if (v > 0) {
+            ALOGI("%s: QUAT_MI2S_RX Audio Mixer MultiMedia%d is On",
+                  __func__, i + 1);
+            return true;
+        }
+    }
+
+    ALOGE("%s: no QUAT_MI2S_RX front end is routed; the mixer path did not "
+          "take effect", __func__);
+    return false;
+}
+
+static void leo_hifi_fallback(struct leo_hifi *lh)
+{
+    /*
+     * Unified fallback.  Stop writing, undo what this generation wrote in
+     * reverse order, and leave the controller in a state that requires a
+     * fresh generation (and a fresh full read-back) before it may claim
+     * HIFI_ACTIVE again.
+     *
+     * The caller (enable_audio_route) is on the select_devices() path; the
+     * actual return to SND_DEVICE_OUT_HEADPHONES happens on the next route
+     * decision, which is why ERROR_FALLBACK is a terminal state until then.
+     */
+    (void) leo_hifi_set_backend(lh);
+    if (lh->vol_applied)
+        (void) leo_hifi_restore_volume_floor(lh);
+
+    lh->generation++;
+    lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_ERROR_FALLBACK;
+    ALOGE("%s: gen=%llu fail=%d evidence=0x%x bypass=0x%x -> error_fallback",
+          __func__, lh->generation, lh->fail_code, lh->evidence, lh->bypass);
 }
+
+void leo_hifi_on_route(struct leo_hifi *lh, bool to_hifi_device)
+{
+    int vol[2];
+
+    if (!to_hifi_device) {
+        /*
+         * Ordinary wired/speaker route.  The WCD chain being live here is
+         * normal and must never be reported as an error.
+         */
+        if (lh->effective == LEO_HIFI_ACTIVE ||
+            lh->effective == LEO_HIFI_DEGRADED ||
+            lh->effective == LEO_HIFI_ARMING ||
+            lh->effective == LEO_HIFI_ERROR_FALLBACK) {
+            lh->generation++;
+            lh->evidence = 0;
+            lh->bypass = 0;
+            lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_WIRED_STANDARD;
+            ALOGI("%s: gen=%llu -> wired_standard", __func__, lh->generation);
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
+    lh->generation++;
+    lh->evidence = 0;
+    lh->bypass = 0;
+    lh->fail_code = LEO_FAIL_NONE;
+    lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_ARMING;
+
+    lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E2;
+    if (lh->supported)
+        lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E3;   /* proven by the probe that let us here */
+    lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E9;
+
+    /* E4: the mixer path really enabled a QUAT front end. */
+    if (leo_quat_front_end_live(lh))
+        lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E4;
+    else
+        lh->fail_code = LEO_FAIL_QUAT_NOT_ROUTED;
+
+    /* E6: the backend was written before the route; confirm it stuck. */
+    if (leo_hifi_set_backend(lh) == 0)
+        lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E6;
+
+    /* E7: the volume control must read back inside the allowed window. */
+    if (leo_hifi_read_volume(lh, vol) == 0 &&
+        vol[0] == vol[1] &&
+        vol[0] >= LEO_HIFI_CTL_FLOOR && vol[0] <= LEO_HIFI_CTL_CEIL)
+        lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E7;
+
+    /* E5: the decisive one -- no complete WCD path to the jack. */
+    if (leo_hifi_check_bypass(lh))
+        lh->evidence |= LEO_EV_E5;
+
+    if ((lh->evidence & LEO_EV_FATAL_MASK) != LEO_EV_FATAL_MASK) {
+        leo_hifi_fallback(lh);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    if ((lh->evidence & LEO_EV_E7) == 0) {
+        lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_DEGRADED;
+        ALOGW("%s: gen=%llu evidence=0x%x bypass=0x%x -> hifi_degraded",
+              __func__, lh->generation, lh->evidence, lh->bypass);
+        return;
+    }
+
+    lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_ACTIVE;
+    ALOGI("%s: gen=%llu evidence=0x%x bypass=0x%x -> hifi_active",
+          __func__, lh->generation, lh->evidence, lh->bypass);
+}
+
+void leo_hifi_on_route_off(struct leo_hifi *lh)
+{
+    lh->generation++;
+    lh->evidence = 0;
+    lh->bypass = 0;
+    lh->effective = LEO_HIFI_IDLE;
+    ALOGI("%s: gen=%llu -> idle", __func__, lh->generation);
+}
+
+void leo_hifi_status_string(struct leo_hifi *lh, char *buf, size_t len)
+{
+    const char *sign = "";
+    int vol0 = -1, vol1 = -1, whole = 0, tenth = 0;
+
+    if (lh->supported && lh->ctl_volume != NULL) {
+        vol0 = mixer_ctl_get_value(lh->ctl_volume, 0);
+        vol1 = mixer_ctl_get_value(lh->ctl_volume, 1);
+    }
+    if (vol0 >= 0)
+        leo_hifi_ctl_to_db(vol0, &sign, &whole, &tenth);
+
+    /*
+     * Unknown values are reported as -1 / "unconfirmed"; we never fill in a
+     * guess.  The UI is required to display "unconfirmed" rather than infer
+     * effective state from requested state.
+     */
+    snprintf(buf, len,
+             "supported=%d;permanent_fail=%d;probes=%d;requested=%s;"
+             "effective=%s;gen=%llu;fail=%d;ev=0x%x;bypass=0x%x;"
+             "vol_ctl_l=%d;vol_ctl_r=%d;vol_db=%s%d.%d;vol_user=%d;"
+             "vol_applied=%d;backend=%s/%s;acdb=absent_expected",
+             lh->supported ? 1 : 0, lh->permanent_fail ? 1 : 0,
+             lh->probe_attempts,
+             lh->requested ? "hifi" : "standard",
+             leo_state_name(lh->effective),
+             lh->generation, lh->fail_code, lh->evidence, lh->bypass,
+             vol0, vol1, sign, whole, tenth, lh->vol_user,
+             lh->vol_applied ? 1 : 0,
+             LEO_HIFI_BITWIDTH_STR, LEO_HIFI_SAMPLERATE_STR);
+}
